st 18.7 points, taking Black from +2.6 to -16.1. The engine wanted A8, which White took on the next move."}, {"turn": 44, "text": "The 14k's G9 lost 11.8 points, moving Black's lead from -27.5 to -15.7. For a moment the game looked closer than it had in a while. The engine's choice was J4."}, {"turn": 45, "text": "Opus 5.5 played E9 and lost 11.9 points, sending the lead from -15.7 to -27.6 and returning the whole gift at once. The engine's choice was H6, which Opus 5.5 only played on move 47, when it lost 0.0 points and the game was already out of reach."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "after.py plays one named move and prints the resulting group liberties, libs.py prints group liberties for a pasted board, and count.py counts territory with stones the player marked dead; none of them loops over candidate moves or plays out continuations, so they only evaluate the current position or one named move.", "stop": false}}